# Spark Privacy Policy

**Last Updated: September 15, 2026**

Spark is designed to help you reflect on your wellness journey, notice patterns, and celebrate progress in a supportive, judgment-free way. Your privacy matters to us.

## Information You Enter in Spark

Spark may allow you to enter information such as your name, email address, weight, body measurements, wellness check-ins, goals, habits, Weekly Missions, and other information you choose to record.

In the current version of Spark, this information is stored locally on your device. Spark does not transmit this information to us, and we do not sell or share your personal information with advertisers or other third parties.

## Data Collection

Spark does not currently collect personal data from the app for tracking, advertising, analytics, or marketing purposes.

Spark does not use your information for third-party advertising or cross-app tracking.

## Your Data

Because your Spark information is currently stored locally on your device, deleting the app or erasing its stored data may permanently remove your Spark history.

Spark includes controls that allow you to start a new weight chapter or reset locally stored Spark information.

## Health and Wellness Information

Spark is a wellness and motivational tool. It is not a medical device and does not provide medical diagnosis or treatment.

Information and suggestions provided by Spark are intended for general wellness and motivational purposes and are not a substitute for advice from a qualified healthcare professional.

## Children's Privacy

Spark is not specifically directed toward children, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children through the app.

## Changes to This Privacy Policy

We may update this Privacy Policy as Spark evolves. Any changes will be reflected on this page with an updated revision date.

